MPAS-Model v8.4.2 fetches NCAR's MMM-physics (tag 20250616-MPASv8.3,
commit a4baf7f3243d1db0dbc5f63473f895bdbdc05c30) into physics_mmm/. The
MPAS physics suites port these schemes from it: the YSU boundary layer
(bl_ysu.F90), the MYNN boundary layer (bl_mynn.F90,
bl_mynn_subroutines.F90, mynn_shared.F90), the YSU orographic
gravity-wave drag (bl_gwdo.F90), the New Tiedtke cumulus scheme
(cu_ntiedtke.F90), WSM6 microphysics (mp_wsm6.F90,
mp_wsm6_effectRad.F90), the radar reflectivity diagnostic (mp_radar.F90),
the MYNN surface layer (sf_mynn.F90) and the revised MM5 surface layer
(sf_sfclayrev.F90). These ports are governed by the licence below (also in
licenses/LICENSE-MMM-physics-BSD-3-Clause.txt).

Numerical Recipes. mp_radar.F90 carries the line

    !(C) Copr. 1986-92 Numerical Recipes Software 2.02

at line 311, inside its GAMMLN log-gamma routine (mp_radar.F90:309-342).
src/hexcore/mpasphys/wsm6_v842.py transcribes that routine (the standard
Lanczos g=5, n=6 coefficients and their evaluation) for WSM6's radar
reflectivity constants, because native MPAS computes them that way and
the port matches native MPAS bit for bit. Those constants feed only the
10 cm reflectivity diagnostic; no prognostic field depends on them.
Numerical Recipes code is licensed to book purchasers and is not
generally redistributable. This material reaches gpuwm-hex through
MMM-physics' BSD-3-Clause release, which cannot dispose of Numerical
Recipes' claim, so the line is preserved here, as MMM-physics and WRF
preserve it. The routine arrived in WRF's public-domain release and has
shipped there, in mp_radar, for about twenty years. gpuwm states the same
position for its own transcriptions of the routine, in the Numerical
Recipes notice of gpuwm's own licence folder. That is a stated reliance,
not a licence; this project keeps it so that WSM6's reflectivity stays
bitwise with native MPAS. The remedy, if the reliance is not
acceptable, is a correctly rounded log-gamma in place of GAMMLN; it would
change WSM6's 10 cm reflectivity and end its bitwise match with native
MPAS for that field, and nothing else.

