9. RRFS (NOAA) -- the fork's dynamical core, and its NOAA GSL physics
==========================================================================

RRFS v2 runs NOAA GSL's fork of MPAS-Model (github.com/RRFSx/MPAS-Model,
commit 1d6e370e7b43a332074809f170532a216c2212fb, "MPAS-v8.3.1-2.26"), pinned
by NOAA EMC's rrfs-workflow (github.com/NOAA-EMC/rrfs-workflow, branch
rrfs-mpas-jedi, commit 08eee4ceee301898d3cb837e03699a8da0d1cb32). The fork
carries the same LICENSE file as MPAS-Model, byte for byte, so section 1
covers what gpuwm-hex ports from it: the fork's dynamical core, a separate
selectable core (the *_rrfs.py modules), and its physics driver layer
(src/hexcore/mpasphys/rrfs/).

The RRFS stage (the fork's suites: --physics-suite hrrrv5 and the rrfs_*
suites) ports the fork's NOAA physics (physics_noaa) to CUDA. Supported
resident table entries run without a native library by default; the native
comparison backend uses the user's own build of the fork. At the fork's
pins they are NCAR/TEMPO 9adf9ef (Apache-2.0), NCAR/MYNN-EDMF c942418, NCAR/MYNN-SFC
b66187f, NOAA-GSL/RUCLSM 8c9f1a8, NOAA-GSL/GFL bf6a4b0, NOAA-GSL/SMOKE
9652bbf and NOAA-GSL/UGWP c1c893e. Apart from TEMPO they carry no licence
file at those pins (MYNN-EDMF added Apache-2.0 upstream on 2026-09-30, after
its pin); gpuwm-hex treats them, like UGWP (section 8), as works of the US
Government (NOAA GSL), by the project's ruling of 2026-10-14. Credit for
each scheme belongs to NOAA GSL, NCAR and their authors. Their hex ports,
UGWP's included (section 8), ship under that ruling, with this attribution. The fork's Noah-MP is under UCAR's terms
(section 4): it stays withheld, and an RRFS stage run that selects
sf_noahmp is refused unless it names them with --licence-opt-in ucar-noahmp.

The ArWen route's RRFS-shaped suite (rrfs_v2_dev) runs gpuwm's WRF-lineage
