10. ArWen (Python package "gpuwm") -- Apache-2.0, a dependency
==========================================================================

The default physics, and the shared device maths the MPAS suites compile
with, come from ArWen, a separate distribution under the Apache License,
Version 2.0, with its own NOTICE covering the WRF-, RRTMG-, RRTMGP-,
Noah-MP-, CORE-MATH-, Arm- and FDLIBM-derived material it carries. Its
default land surface is the WRF-lineage Noah-MP v4.x of section 4 (WRF
public-domain notice). It is declared as a dependency and installed from its own distribution.
Compiled kernel packs also contain copies of its device code (section 16).

ArWen's RTE+RRTMGP radiation, which the global rows' gpuwm-global arm runs
(as does any ArWen-route run that selects it), reads a trace-gas and ozone
table that gpuwm's data package ships under CC-BY-SA-4.0. gpuwm-hex does not
carry it. It is data: the licence permits sale, and its share-alike reaches
only adaptations of that table.

